_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/26","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/26","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/26/labels","id":16503691,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A-9OL","number":26,"title":"4.9","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":50,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-06-24T20:03:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T15:30:45Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-05T22:28:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T01:43:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124204","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124204.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124204.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Supersedes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124157\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124157 was technically a good change, minus the AI comments and commit description. I am opening a PR myself since it is less work and less annoying to make a PR for this tiny change than it is to try to prompt someone else's LLM into doing things correctly. \r\n\r\nThe main problem comes from the difference in how OpenGL and Direct3D allocate memory. D3D has always been more explicit, while OpenGL uses these buffer hints. \r\n\r\nIn theory `GL_DYNAMIC_DRAW` means \"I am going to update this mesh a lot from the CPU, and I am going to use it for a lot of draw operations\". `GL_DYNAMIC_COPY` means, I am going to update this mesh a lot from the GPU, and I am going to use it for a lot of draw operations\".\r\n\r\nOpenGL drivers takes these hints, but mostly infers the optimal allocation strategy based on usage. Accordingly, on native OpenGL, the hints are almost always ignored. In this case, they are ignored and this PR makes no difference with native GL.\r\n\r\nHowever, on ANGLE, these hints get translated directly to D3D properties and they are treated as explicit instructions. So `GL_DYNAMIC_DRAW` ends up storing the mesh data in CPU accessible memory despite the memory never needing to be accessed by the CPU. This leads to worse performance than when running with native OpenGL. \r\n\r\nSwitching to `GL_DYNAMIC_COPY` resolves this issue without changing behaviour. Notably, particles were already correctly using `GL_DYNAMIC_COPY`\r\n\r\nTo test, I modified the Godot platformer demo to have 50 animated characters\r\n\r\nTested on Windows 11 computer with a Ryzen 5 9600X CPU and an RTX 4080 GPU. Exact results vary depending on the hardware. \r\n**Master (GL): 560 FPS**\r\n**Master (ANGLE): 100 FPS**\r\n**This PR (GL): 560 FPS**\r\n**This PR (ANGLE): 220 FPS**","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124204/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124204/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}